@startuml uc_gestion_apps
' Cas d'utilisation — cycle de vie des applications
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #F7F9FC
  BorderColor #2C3E50
}
skinparam actorStyle awesome
left to right direction

actor "MEMBER" as MEMBER
actor "CLIENT_ADMIN" as CADMIN
actor "ADMIN" as ADMIN
actor "Knative Serving" as KNATIVE <<système>>
actor "Ordonnanceur\nCrashLoopScheduler" as SCHED <<système>>

rectangle "Gestion des applications" {

  usecase "Déployer une application\nPOST /api/apps" as UC_CREATE
  usecase "Lister ses applications\nGET /api/apps" as UC_LIST
  usecase "Consulter le détail d'une application\nGET /api/apps/{id}" as UC_GET
  usecase "Redéployer\nPOST /api/apps/{id}/deploy" as UC_REDEPLOY
  usecase "Modifier et redéployer\nPUT /api/apps/{id}" as UC_UPDATE
  usecase "Supprimer une application\nDELETE /api/apps/{id}" as UC_DELETE
  usecase "Lister les révisions\nGET /api/apps/{id}/revisions" as UC_REV
  usecase "Revenir à une révision\nPOST /api/apps/{id}/rollback/{revision}" as UC_ROLLBACK

  usecase "Créer le namespace tenant\net la NetworkPolicy d'isolation" as UC_NS
  usecase "Créer/Recréer le Knative Service" as UC_KSVC
  usecase "Câbler automatiquement\nKafkaSource + Trigger" as UC_WIRE
  usecase "Synchroniser le statut réel\ndepuis Kubernetes" as UC_SYNC
  usecase "Détecter les CrashLoopBackOff\net alerter" as UC_CRASH
  usecase "Journaliser l'opération\n(DeploymentLog + SSE)" as UC_LOG

  usecase "Forcer la suppression d'une app\nDELETE /api/admin/apps/{id}" as UC_FORCE
  usecase "Suspendre / restaurer une app\n(scale max=0 / restauration)" as UC_SUSPEND
  usecase "Lister toutes les applications\nGET /api/admin/apps" as UC_ALL
}

MEMBER --> UC_CREATE
MEMBER --> UC_LIST
MEMBER --> UC_GET
MEMBER --> UC_REDEPLOY
MEMBER --> UC_UPDATE
MEMBER --> UC_DELETE
MEMBER --> UC_REV
MEMBER --> UC_ROLLBACK
CADMIN --|> MEMBER

ADMIN --> UC_FORCE
ADMIN --> UC_SUSPEND
ADMIN --> UC_ALL

SCHED --> UC_CRASH
KNATIVE --> UC_SYNC

UC_CREATE   ..> UC_NS    : <<include>>
UC_CREATE   ..> UC_KSVC  : <<include>>
UC_CREATE   ..> UC_LOG   : <<include>>
UC_CREATE   ..> UC_WIRE  : <<extend>> si kafkaEnabled
UC_UPDATE   ..> UC_KSVC  : <<include>>
UC_REDEPLOY ..> UC_KSVC  : <<include>>
UC_DELETE   ..> UC_LOG   : <<include>>
UC_LIST     ..> UC_SYNC  : <<include>>
UC_GET      ..> UC_SYNC  : <<include>>
UC_ALL      ..> UC_SYNC  : <<include>>
UC_CRASH    ..> UC_LOG   : <<include>>
UC_ROLLBACK ..> UC_LOG   : <<include>>

note right of UC_CREATE
  Permission requise : DEPLOY_APP
  (idem redeploy / update / rollback).
  DELETE_APP pour la suppression.
  Aucun quota bloquant sur le nombre d'apps.
end note

note right of UC_DELETE
  Suppression logique : status = "DELETED"
  afin de préserver l'historique de facturation ;
  le Knative Service et les CR d'eventing
  sont réellement supprimés du cluster.
end note

' Classes utilisées : App, AppRequest, AppResponse, DeploymentLog
' Contrôleurs utilisés : AppController, AdminController
' Services utilisés : AppService, AppDeploymentAsyncRunner, KnativeService, KnativeWatcher, CrashLoopScheduler, EventingService, LogSseService, UserContextService, PermissionService
' Pourquoi ces éléments apparaissent : chaque cas correspond à une méthode publique d'AppController/AdminController ; les cas « système » correspondent au watcher, au scheduler et à syncStatusFromKubernetes().
' Fichiers sources vérifiés :
'   app/AppController.java:27-84 (8 endpoints, gardes DEPLOY_APP / DELETE_APP)
'   app/AppService.java:39-73 (createApp), :77-91 (listApps/listAllApps), :99-124 (syncStatusFromKubernetes),
'                      :136-168 (updateApp/redeploy), :172-184 (deleteApp → status DELETED), :188-200 (revisions/rollback), :207-236 (checkCrashLoops)
'   app/CrashLoopScheduler.java:11-17 (@Scheduled fixedRate = 5 min)
'   app/KnativeService.java:149-190 (deploy), :199 (scaleService), :245 (delete), :368 (listRevisions), :396 (rollbackToRevision)
'   app/AppDeploymentAsyncRunner.java:48-63 (câblage Kafka automatique)
'   admin/AdminController.java:98-116 (getAllApps, forceDeleteApp), :414 (restore), :440-472 (suspend/restore client)
' Divergence relevée : la suppression n'efface pas la ligne en base (soft delete via status="DELETED"), et le rollback ne crée pas de log SSE différent — il réutilise addLog(type="ROLLBACK").
@enduml
